                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="608-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>MXL 990S</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The MXL 990S is essentially a 990 with the addition of a switchable pad (-10dB) and high-pass filter (-6dB/octave @ 150Hz). As part of the &#8220;900 Series,&#8221; the 990S is sold exclusively through Guitar Center and its affiliates. </p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/mxl/MXL-990S-770.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/mxl/MXL-990S-770-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="MXL 770 and 990S" width="200" /></a>Aside from the finish colors and the height of the microphone, the MXL 770 is identical to the 990S. The two mics&#8217; MSRPs, as of late 2012, are the same ($150).</p><p>The capsule assembly in the 990S can be found in the 770, 990, and MCA SP-1. It is MXL&#8217;s 603S/604 small-diaphragm model mounted within a brass baffle ring. The brass ring alters the capsule&#8217;s frequency and polar response.</p><p>The suspended area of the diaphragm has a 17mm diameter, with a 20mm backplate. The housing that contains these pieces has a 22mm diameter. See the <a href="/microphones/tag/603s">603S capsule listing</a> for more mics with the same capsule.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/mxl/770-990S-pcb.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/mxl/770-990S-pcb-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="MXL 770 and 990S PCBs" width="200" /></a>The 770/990S circuit is a variation on the Schoeps transformerless design. A simpler version, with no pad and filter, is found in the MXL 990, MCA SP-1, MXL 2006, and MXL V63M.</p><p>The MXL 990S ships in a padded rigid plastic case with an elastic shockmount.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/MXL/990S">MXL 990S</a> is also known as: 990-S.</p>
